      "body": {
        "blocks": [
          {
            "type": "paragraph",
            "text": "A biologist studied the heights of 9 different plants of the same species. The heights of the plants are 56cm, 65cm, 74cm, 75cm, 76cm, 77cm, 80cm, 81cm and 91cm."
          },
          {
            "type": "list",
            "ordered": false,
            "items": [
              "Step1: Find the mean.",
              "Step2: Subtract the mean from each data point to find the deviation of each point.",
              "Step3: Square the result of each deviation which eliminates negative values and emphasizes larger deviations.",
              "Step4: Find the average of the squared deviations.",
              "Step5: Take the square root of the result from step 4. This is the standard deviation."
            ],
            "bold": [
              "Step1",
              "Step2",
              "Step3",
              "Step4",
              "Step5"
            ]
          },
          {
            "type": "table",
            "caption": "Table: Calculation of standard deviation for plant heights",
            "header": [
              "Height in (cm) xᵢ",
              "Mean µ",
              "Subtract mean from each data point (xᵢ - µ)",
              "Square the result of each deviation (xᵢ - µ)²",
              "Sum of squared deviations ∑(xᵢ - µ)²",
              "Variance (Average of the squared deviations) ∑(xᵢ - µ)²/N",
              "Standard deviation σ = √(∑(xᵢ - µ)²/N)"
            ],
